(611, 2, '2013-09-16 17:47:32', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 'Solstice Celebration - What to Expect?', '', 'draft', 'open', 'open', '', '', '', '', '2013-09-16 17:47:32', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 0, 'http://humanistculture.com/?p=611', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(612, 2, '2013-09-21 20:21:55', '2013-09-21 20:21:55', '<p><span style=\"font-size:16.52px;line-height:1.5em;\">[youtube=http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VDCN6I1n6o4]<br />\n</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16.52px;line-height:1.5em;\">This is the song that eventually led to the Winter Solstice, and humanistculture.com</span></p>\n<p>For years, I had been looking for a humanist anthem, that resonated with everything I believed and made me proud to be a member of my species. There were plenty of great songs that almost hit the mark, but nothing that quite made me feel the way I wanted to.</p>\n<p>Eventually I realized, if I couldn\'t find what I was looking for, I could just write it myself.<!--more--></p>\n<p>At the time, I had no idea I was about to embark on a quest to jumpstart a revitalized movement of humanist art and music, or reimagine a holiday. And it turns out, starting out your quest by writing the central anthem for a movement isn\'t the greatest idea - central anthems are *hard*. Who knew? And when I started, I didn\'t know anything about writing songs for communal singing.</p>\n<p>But I\'ve been fine-tuning this song for two years now. This is a rough mix of the final, recorded version, to be released towards the end of January as we finish our album.</p>\n', 'Brighter Than Today', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'brighter-than-today', '', '', '2013-09-21 20:21:55', '2013-09-21 20:21:55', '', 0, 'http://humanistculture.com/?p=612', 0, 'post', '', 0),
