(921, 2, '2014-08-23 21:54:57', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '<em>You\'re wandering in a desert. You\'re looking for something. You don\'t know how to find it. You have a few maps, cobbled together, that sort of point you in the right direction. </em><em>The wind and sand bite at your face. You swelter under the sun during the day, and the huddle under your blankets, shivering, at night.</em>\n\n<em>You feel very alone.</em>\n\n<em>Periodically you find an oasis in the desert, or a lone traveller heading another direction. They take a look at your cobbled together map, and they see a blank spot on it and say \"oh, yes, in this spot, there is a forgotten culture worth visiting. In this other spot, there be dragons. Be cautious.\"</em>\n\n<em>They ask where you\'re going. You tell them your final destination. And...</em>\n\n<em>...they look at you, sort of confused. Perhaps they ask a question or two. Then, inevitably, they shrug and wish you well on your journey.</em>\n\n<em>It\'s that shrug that makes you feel especially alone.</em>\n\n&nbsp;\n\nLast month, I went to the Effective Altruism Summit.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nOne night, you huddle by your campfire. The stars are pretty, but feel so fragile and far away. Your stapled-together-map fragments are looking especially confusing, and you\'re about to just give up.\n\nAnd then a stranger approaches. Tentativel', 'A yea', '', 'draft', 'open', 'open', '', '', '', '', '2014-08-23 21:54:57', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '', 0, 'http://humanistculture.com/?p=921', 0, 'post', '', 0),
